s is basically what Neymar  wanted from the beginning the king  originally went to war with wakanda  because they refused to turn over Riri  Williams a young scientist who built the  vibranium detecting apparatus nor they  agreed to go to war with him against the  surface world yet this truth signifies  that they may be willing to align with  talukan in the future should they ever  find themselves under attack Time  Magazine has stated that Neymar will be  returning though they seem to be basing  this more in the position that Neymar  finds himself in at the end of the movie  rather than any official announcement  from Marvel it definitely does seem like  we'll be seeing more of the character  and that would be as opportunistic as  his Comics counterparts Neymar made his  comics debut in 1939 in Motion Picture  Funny's weekly issue 1. in his first  appearance Neymar viciously attacks a  crew of a salvage vessel trying to bring  up lost treasure this is followed by  Neymar's mother telling him the story of  why they don't trust surface dwellers  some of them attacked Atlantis and  killed many of their people so even in  his brutal first appearance Neymar's  actions can be justified as defending  his Nation May more often switched his  size between heroes and villains and  never really settles down as one or the  other in 1964's X-Men Issue 6 agnito  tries to get Neymar to join his  Brotherhood of evil mutants but Neymar  quickly becomes disenchanted with  magneso's leadership and turns on him in  dark Avengers issue 8 Neymar joins the  X-Men but even in his time as a member  of a superhero team Namor is morally  ambiguous in Avengers vs X-Men issue 8  May more floods wakanda during a  conflict with the Avengers interference  of direct orders from Cyclops that scene  was clearly an inspiration for one of  Neymar's more malicious acts in wakanda  Forever it's hard to call the mcu's  version of Neymar good or evil either it  does some extreme things but in the name  of 